GajpfA&_nc_oc=AdqOhoWZEMjBjFlDUMkqxm-aOMqb-ZgnimlpoiaDZGISrj8hRskrhPeUeJYf_9cjqvU&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f30f&oh=00_AQWgOodEUKecOXwHBGxWuq6gI3yREcatV0ETJHN7cQd5oA&oe=6B0F148E"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "DUET Human Body 360", "keywords": ["biology", "anatomy", "science", "education"], "long_description": "DUET Human Body 360 is a life-size, see-through human body that students study in VR or in their own room.\n\n- Explore 2,400 parts: point at any bone, muscle, organ, vessel, nerve or gland to see its name and job, and hear a teacher explain how it works.\n- Organ Lab: large detailed models of the heart, eye, ear, brain, lungs, kidney, tooth and skin, with 61 guided steps: blood through the heart's chambers, light focusing in the eye, sound travelling through the ear and more.\n- Journeys: follow air from the nose to every cell, food from the mouth to energy and waste, and blood around the body, step by step.\n- Take apart: organs and bones float out of the body, labelled.\n- Put-back game: grab each organ or bone and return it to its place.\n- Teacher voice and text in English, Hindi and Hinglish.\n- Works offline after the first launch.\n\nFor schools: full access comes with a DUET STEM school subscription code. Without a code, a free 10-minute demo is available every day.", "short_description": "Step inside a see-through 3D human body: every bone, organ, vessel and nerve named and explained, with organs shown working, for school students in English, Hindi and Hinglish."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://ashutoshduet.github.io/duet-lms-media/body/privacy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "DUET Power", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://ashutoshduet.github.io/duet-lms-media/body/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873"